{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>These are the heads of their fathers' houses.</b> It is fitting to count these as princes over Israel, for they were the most distinguished of the nation. This is because Reuben was the firstborn of Israel, and among his descendants there were no men worthy of being named other than his sons mentioned here, who were included among the seventy souls who had already died, as he explained in saying: וַיָּמָת יוֹסֵף וְכָל אֶחָיו וְגוֹ׳ (Exodus 1:6). And so it was with the sons of Simeon. But Levi, who outlived them all, also raised his grandsons to understand and to instruct, and likewise Kehath and Amram, so that from them emerged Moses, Aaron, and Miriam."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:37.606524658Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}